    "references: the provider suffix `@file` is stripped from a router's service, a router's middlewares, a service's weighted, mirroring and failover services and a chain (O349), so druidfi/stonehenge's 3 missed pairs are found (ref_recall .9643 to 1); picodotdev/blog-ejemplos writes `service: [nginx-mirroring]` (a sequence, which Traefik does not accept), and the pattern now reads its strings, so fathom draws 1 pair the oracle does not hold (ref_precision 1 to .9882)",
    "rendiffdev/rendiff-dev: restricted to traefik/dynamic.yml, traefik/traefik.yml (-only; the files outside are a disclosed gap, not measured)",
    "route pairs (LB-F168, LB-F169): a route joins the declarations of its nearest compose project (the route file's directory, then each ancestor), one pair for every compose file of that directory that declares the service, read by docker compose config 5.1.4 (--no-consistency); scored by lang-routes under -only, which restricts the measured dialect's files and not the compose files a target joins to; 30 pairs from 7 subjects (ecamp3 9, blog-ejemplos 4, rendiff-dev 4, wikibase-suite 4, opa-traefik-microservice-authz 3, Vistack 3, stonehenge 3), all found and none beyond the truth, every one joined to a compose file Compose read (tier A): fathom's resolver now walks ancestor directories before the repository (O435), so wikibase-suite's routes join its root compose file and not the five overlay stacks. Re-measured 2026-10-24 on Linux: the 2026-10-02 reading held 21 pairs and one Vistack pair joined to a Kubernetes Service read by yaml.v3 (tier C); this run joined Vistack, rendiff-dev and stonehenge routes to compose services and did not reproduce that tier C pair, a difference of the measuring environment not explained here",
    "route references (route_* counts, LB-F98) are scored into xref_precision and xref_recall with the oracle's cross_references: a route, upstream or mesh rule's entity to the Kubernetes Service or compose service its target host names, resolved by fusion.ResolveRouteRefs (the resolver ingest stores route_ref edges from) over the files ingest's route pass reads; route_unresolved_<reason> counts fathom's unresolved references, route_oracle_unresolved_<reason> the oracle's",
    "wmde/wikibase-suite: restricted to config/traefik-dynamic.yml (-only; the files outside are a disclosed gap, not measured)"
